# hakios-mali on the phone (userland/src/mali, darwin/userland/mali27.sh): mali-probe's stages against the kernel's
# HakiosMali, the first time as early as the service is there (it waits up to 60 s for it), before the window server
# has drawn much, then once more with every descriptor printed, once the home screen's GPU work runs beside it. Its
# verdicts go to the console and, as "!!mali-probe:" lines, into what the kernel keeps for the host. Last, a picture of
# what the Metal driver put on the screen (fbgrab -log, tools/log/fbjpg.py LOG OUT.jpg home): the last thing of the run,
# as the log keeps its last 256 KB. For the 27 release's small image: MALI27=$OBJ/mali RC_JOBS=userland/jobs/rc.jobs.maliprobe
# (darwin/mtk27.sh root), boot-arg mali=1 (and metal=1 for the picture).
/hakios/bin/mali-probe
/hakios/bin/rwtouch wait 90
/hakios/bin/mali-probe --dump
/hakios/bin/rwtouch wait 290
/hakios/bin/fbgrab -log home
/hakios/bin/rwtouch wait 120
